# tools/live-check profile — any OpenID Connect IdP through the template's
# generic `federations.oidc` entry (Okta, Clerk, Entra ID, Auth0, Keycloak …).
#
#   cp oidc.env.example okta.env         # one copy per IdP; *.env is git-ignored
#   tools/live-check/live-check.sh start okta
#
# The IdP's client needs this exact redirect URI (LIVE_CHECK_PORT, 3210 by default):
#
#   http://localhost:3210/session/oauth/federation/oidc/callback
#
# LIVE_CHECK_EXPECTED_ISS is what the callback's RFC 9207 `iss` must equal —
# for an OIDC IdP that is its issuer, byte for byte. Leave it empty to record
# whatever arrives without judging it (an IdP whose metadata does not advertise
# `authorization_response_iss_parameter_supported` may send none, and the
# provider then does not require one).
#
# Not yet exercised against a real IdP — the Google profile is. The first run
# against one goes into its issue, and this comment goes away.
LIVE_CHECK_FEDERATION=oidc
LIVE_CHECK_EXPECTED_ISS=
FEDERATIONS_OIDC_ISSUER=
FEDERATIONS_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
FEDERATIONS_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
